# Docker build context exclusions.
# Without this, `target/` (14 GB+) and node_modules ship to the remote
# builder on every deploy and turn a 5-minute build into a half-hour one.

# Rust build artifacts (cargo caches inside the image instead)
target/
**/target/

# Node / pnpm
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
**/.pnpm-store/

# Frontend build output (rebuilt inside the image when needed; the cloud
# server image doesn't ship the desktop UI bundle anyway)
crates/hoard-desktop/ui/dist/
crates/hoard-desktop/ui/build/
crates/hoard-desktop/ui/.svelte-kit/

# Tauri build output
crates/hoard-desktop/src-tauri/target/

# Git + local config (we still need .git when cargo wants vcs metadata,
# but Fly's distroless runtime never needs it, so keep .git out of context)
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.githooks/

# The AI layer and the session notes. `.local/` never leaves this machine, and
# a remote builder is off it: the context is uploaded whole even though only
# the binary survives into the image.
.local/
.claude/

# Secrets and local env. The bare names only match at the context root, and
# the context is the whole repo (`COPY . .` in the builder stage), so without
# the `**/` forms `deploy/.env.discord-bot` and `web/.env` rode along to the
# remote builder on every deploy. They never reached the runtime image, but a
# builder layer cache is still somewhere a token should not be.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs (not consumed by the build)
docs/
*.md
!Cargo.lock
!Cargo.toml

# Local data + temp
data/
tmp/
*.log
